From: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dsi: add Matisse fixed-color link diagnostics

The controlled native DSI pattern produces thin visible stripes on the
LCD, but a complete image has not passed physical acceptance. Add fixed
blue, green, red and white pattern choices using the existing VID_FIXED
selector, to distinguish the general pattern's geometry from link issues.

Commands3..6 choose fixed colors. Power/modeset/command serialization and
peripheral interrupt masking from the previous diagnostic remain in use.
This is an opt-in diagnostic, not a production display interface.

Signed-off-by: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_host.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_host.c
index f28db30a1..9185d8cae 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_host.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_host.c
@@ -2787,7 +2787,7 @@ static int matisse_link_diag_set(void *data, u64 command)
 		DSI_IRQ_MASK_BTA_DONE | DSI_IRQ_MASK_ERROR;
 	int ret = 0;
 
-	if (command > 2)
+	if (command > 6)
 		return -EINVAL;
 
 	drm_modeset_lock_all(msm_host->dev);
@@ -2813,6 +2813,19 @@ static int matisse_link_diag_set(void *data, u64 command)
 		clocks = dsi_read(msm_host, REG_DSI_CLK_CTRL);
 		dsi_sw_reset(msm_host);
 		dsi_write(msm_host, REG_DSI_CLK_CTRL, clocks);
+	} else if (command >= 3) {
+		static const u32 colors[] = {
+			0x0000ff, 0x00ff00, 0xff0000, 0xffffff,
+		};
+
+		dsi_write(msm_host, REG_DSI_TEST_PATTERN_GEN_VIDEO_INIT_VAL,
+			  colors[command - 3]);
+		dsi_write(msm_host, REG_DSI_TPG_VIDEO_CONFIG,
+			  DSI_TPG_VIDEO_CONFIG_BPP(VIDEO_CONFIG_24BPP) |
+			  DSI_TPG_VIDEO_CONFIG_RGB);
+		dsi_write(msm_host, REG_DSI_TEST_PATTERN_GEN_CTRL,
+			  DSI_TEST_PATTERN_GEN_CTRL_VIDEO_PATTERN_SEL(VID_FIXED) |
+			  DSI_TEST_PATTERN_GEN_CTRL_EN);
 	} else if (command == 1) {
 		msm_dsi_host_test_pattern_en(&msm_host->base);
 	} else {
